WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.770
You may not be as speedy as him, but you'll
certainly want to race as fast as you can

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.740
to see Sonic the Hedgehog on the silver screen
next year.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.800
Looper recently spoke with Sonic the Hedgehog
composer Tom Holkenborg, also known as Junkie

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.840
XL, who has scored films like Deadpool, Batman
v Superman: Dawn of Justice, Mad Max: Fury

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.080
Road, Alita: Battle Angel, and the newly released
Terminator: Dark Fate.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.900
In conversation, we asked if there was anything
about Sonic that Holkenborg could tease — without

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.220
spilling spoilers, of course.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.560
Holkenborg had some promising words to share:

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.160
"The only thing I can say is that it turned
out to be a really, really great film, and

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.500
it's so much fun to work on it.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.860
Really great characters.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.400
Really lovely, really cute at the same time.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.579
So I'm looking forward for that to finish."

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:48.530
Anticipation for the project, based on Sega's
beloved video game franchise of the same name,

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:53.130
has been palpable from the minute Paramount
Pictures announced in October 2017 that it

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.280
would be fast tracking the film to development.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.870
Hype continued to build in February 2018,
when Paramount confirmed Sonic the Hedgehog

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.720
would race into cinemas in November 2019.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.660
Fans finally got their first look at the long-awaited
movie in a trailer that was released in April,

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.160
2019.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.400
"Ahhhh!"

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.080
"AHHHHH!!!!"

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.880
When that footage finally arrived, however,
reception was mixed at best and shockingly

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:15.820
bad at worst.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:20.420
The majority of fans felt that the most important
component of Sonic the Hedgehog, Sonic himself,

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:22.980
lacked a certain something in his design.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.640
As a CGI character interacting with humans
like Jim Carrey's villainous super-scientist

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:32.540
Dr. Robotnik and James Marsden's friendly
Montana sheriff Tom Wachowski, Sonic needed

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.880
to look picture-perfect.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.920
Many fans weren't completely satisfied with
the way Sonic appeared in the first trailer

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:43.190
for the film, and Paramount took the criticisms
in stride before making an important decision.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:47.659
Shortly after the unveiling of the first Sonic
the Hedgehog trailer, director Jeff Fowler

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.160
announced that the special effects team would
be going back to the drawing board to give

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.740
Sonic a design overhaul.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.360
He tweeted in May 2019:

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.760
"Thank you for the support.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.820
And the criticism.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.420
The message is loud and clear... you aren't
happy with the design &amp; you want changes.

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:02.460
It's going to happen.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.680
Everyone at Paramount &amp; Sega are fully committed
to making this character the BEST he can be."

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.600
The filmmaker subsequently confirmed that
the redesign would delay the film, which is

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.620
now slated to open in theaters on February
14, 2020.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.800
Since then, we've seen peeks of what could
be a possible Sonic redesign floating around

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.600
online, with one photo even showing the new
Sonic on an in-theater promotional standee.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.520
The snaps suggest that the Sonic the Hedgehog
team has done a bang-up job improving the

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.560
character's appearance.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:33.980
In fact, it looks like the design team were
quickly able to give fans basically everything

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.980
they could want from the reworked design.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.880
The conversation surrounding the original
Sonic design was mixed, at best.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.440
Some fans seemed to delight in collectively
roasting the character's original movie design,

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.900
poking fun at his creepy human teeth and odd
body proportions.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.300
While some fans were somewhat more positive,
that still left Paramount with a pretty clear

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.920
indication that fans weren't going to be happy.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.350
When the photos of the alleged redesign surfaced
on social media, many who were initially critical

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:04.160
of Sonic the Hedgehog changed their tune,
complimenting the new design and admitting

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.800
that they were keen to see the film.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.680
One even wrote on Twitter that the purported
visual update Sonic received looks so incredible

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:14.950
that other teams handling Sonic-related content
and products could stand to learn a thing

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:17.120
or two from the Sonic the Hedgehog film team.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:17.780
They wrote,

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:22.140
"[Movie Sonic's] redesign is so good it even
makes the modern sonic design from the games

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.480
look bland in comparison."

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:28.260
It's clear that everyone involved with Sonic
the Hedgehog is working fast to create a satisfying

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.160
final product.

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:33.420
And based on what Tom Holkenborg told us,
the film is going to be more than worth it

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.020
in the end.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:38.260
Sonic the Hedgehog will hit theaters on February
14, 2020.

